{
  "info": {
    "name": "WgCards Sandbox API",
    "description": "Sandbox smoke tests for the WgCards API (V3.0.8) described in the CardCove multi-supplier integration plan. Every request/response body is AES/ECB/PKCS7 encrypted with the caller's appId (UTF-8 bytes) as the raw AES key - handled automatically by the pre-request/test scripts on each request via Postman's built-in CryptoJS. Run 'Get Token' first (its Tests script stores the token into the collection variable used by every other request).\n\nNote from the doc: 'Only addresses in the ip whitelist can be successfully accessed' - if every request times out, confirm the machine running Postman is whitelisted with WgCards, not just that credentials are correct.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "host", "value": "http://121.43.36.102:9009" },
    { "key": "appId", "value": "2025112058411324" },
    { "key": "accountId", "value": "2025112058411325" },
    { "key": "appKey", "value": "o%Cmiq52TP4o06Uok&R6tC#^#FXGNE*3" },
    { "key": "token", "value": "" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Get Token",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const CryptoJS = require('crypto-js');",
              "function aesKey(appId) { return CryptoJS.enc.Utf8.parse(appId); }",
              "function encryptMsg(appId, obj) {",
              "  const key = aesKey(appId);",
              "  return CryptoJS.AES.encrypt(JSON.stringify(obj), key, { mode: CryptoJS.mode.ECB, padding: CryptoJS.pad.Pkcs7 }).toString();",
              "}",
              "const appId = pm.collectionVariables.get('appId');",
              "const accountId = pm.collectionVariables.get('accountId');",
              "const appKey = pm.collectionVariables.get('appKey');",
              "const payload = { appId, appKey };",
              "const body = { appId, accountId, msg: encryptMsg(appId, payload) };",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('requestBody', JSON.stringify(body));"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const CryptoJS = require('crypto-js');",
              "function aesKey(appId) { return CryptoJS.enc.Utf8.parse(appId); }",
              "function decryptMsg(appId, b64) {",
              "  const key = aesKey(appId);",
              "  return CryptoJS.AES.decrypt(b64, key, { mode: CryptoJS.mode.ECB, padding: CryptoJS.pad.Pkcs7 }).toString(CryptoJS.enc.Utf8);",
              "}",
              "const appId = pm.collectionVariables.get('appId');",
              "pm.test('HTTP 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "let raw = pm.response.text().trim();",
              "if (raw.startsWith('\"')) raw = JSON.parse(raw);",
              "let decrypted;",
              "try { decrypted = JSON.parse(decryptMsg(appId, raw)); } catch (e) { console.log('decrypt failed', e.message); }",
              "console.log('Decrypted response:', decrypted);",
              "pm.test('code === 200', () => pm.expect(decrypted && decrypted.code).to.eql(200));",
              "if (decrypted && decrypted.data) {",
              "  pm.collectionVariables.set('token', decrypted.data);",
              "  console.log('Token stored:', decrypted.data);",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
        "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{{requestBody}}", "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } } },
        "url": { "raw": "{{host}}/api/getToken", "host": ["{{host}}"], "path": ["api", "getToken"] },
        "description": "Rate limit: 40 requests / 60s. No auth headers required - this is what issues the 2h bearer token."
      }
    },
